CopyLingo

The per-kanji readings in the Japanese seed data (the "kanji_readings" key of
vocabulary payloads in cmd/seeding/data/ja/*.json) are derived from the
following resources and are distributed under the same licence,
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0):

- KANJIDIC2 and JMdict, by the Electronic Dictionary Research and Development
  Group (EDRDG). https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html
- JmdictFurigana, by Doublevil, derived from JMdict.
  https://github.com/Doublevil/JmdictFurigana

They are generated by scripts/gen_kanji_readings.py. The Korean 훈음 in their
"hun_eum" field are this project's own, from scripts/kanji_hun_eum.tsv.
